# Code quality

- **Simplicity first.** No "just in case" abstractions (YAGNI).
- **DRY.** Extract logic duplicated in two or more places.
- **Explicit over clever.** Readable, obvious code wins.
- **Descriptive names.** Prefer `getActiveUserSessions` over `getSessions`.
- **One concept per file.** Split when a file does two jobs.
- **No dead or commented-out code.** No `TODO` without a linked issue.
- **Doc-comment exported symbols** (what and why, not how).
- **Typed boundaries.** Strictest typing available. In TypeScript: strict mode,
  no `any` (use `unknown` + narrowing). Validate structured data at boundaries
  with a schema; derive types from the schema.
- **Error handling on every external call.** Never swallow errors. User-facing
  failures get clear messages.
- **Change only what the task requires.** No drive-by refactors or dependency
  bumps in the same change.
- **Read before you edit.** Match existing conventions in the file.
- **Writing style:** no em dashes, no emojis (code, docs, commits, PRs, chat).
- **Commits:** Conventional Commits, atomic, concise, no PII, no ticket IDs or
  URLs in messages, no AI attribution trailers. Agents may commit and push.
